40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">5\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/7a/DFF_Start.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209045748\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"DFF Start\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Start.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Start.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/7a/DFF_Start.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209045748\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">6\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">7\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Multichain at D2 or D4 to get them all, a Jump Chain at D3 will also work but that red emblem is incredibly painful to take - it disables all your equipment. Ouch. Squall is our Assist now, swap out boosters appropriately. Remember how awesome his Solid Barrel is and use Rush Impact to slam the opponent into the ground so he can use it. The KP Chance is a 90 second win.\n</p><p>First is a Delusory Warlock with Rising Wave and Float System. Next is a Fallacious Tree with Black Hole, Vacuum Wave, Force to Courage, and Moogle. Then it's Party time, the players are a Phantasmal Girl with Blizzara and Flood, an Imaginary Champion with Transience, Sudden Cruelty, Force to Courage and Moogle, and a Counterfeit Wraith with Tentacle of Spite (ground spin attack and large energy orb), Tentacle of Spite (aerial wall rush and energy orb barrage), Force to Courage, and Moogle.\n</p><p>The chest has Oerba Beads for us.\n</p><p>Go to the Moogle and buy a Jump skill and Multichain, if you don't have one. Head back through the teleport to the Land of Discord, suddenly there are four orbs here to get a chain skill from. There's also a Level 20 Imaginary Champion to deal with. Unfortunately there are no new chests in the region, so gather the orbs and head into the newly active gateway nearby.\n<br style=\"clear:both\" />\n</p>\n<table class=\"D012 board\" style=\"float:right\">\n\n<tbody><tr bgcolor=\"068FB0\">\n<td width=\"19px;background:white\">&#160;\n</td>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">A\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">B\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">C\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">D\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">E\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">F\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">G\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">H\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">1\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234631\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Mu Fur\"><img alt=\"Mu Fur\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Chest.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Chest.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/40?cb=20110203234631\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">2\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/1/1e/DFF_Expert_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110204003912\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"False Stalwart\"><img alt=\"False Stalwart\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"25\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Expert Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Expert_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/1/1e/DFF_Expert_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/25?cb=20110204003912\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">3\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">4\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/7a/DFF_Start.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209045748\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"DFF Start\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Start.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Start.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/7a/DFF_Start.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209045748\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234241\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Imaginary Champion\"><img alt=\"Imaginary Champion\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"16\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/16?cb=20110203234241\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/1/13/D012_Emblem_Purple.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209050509\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Initial BRV Boost for both\"><img alt=\"Initial BRV Boost for both\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"D012 Emblem Purple.png\" data-image-key=\"D012_Emblem_Purple.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/1/13/D012_Emblem_Purple.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209050509\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234241\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Delusory Warlock\"><img alt=\"Delusory Warlock\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"16\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/16?cb=20110203234241\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/8/86/DFF_Chaos_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203235702\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Exdeath\"><img alt=\"Exdeath\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"36\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Chaos Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Chaos_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/8/86/DFF_Chaos_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/36?cb=20110203235702\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">5\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/5f/D012_Party_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20121006224522\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Party Battle\"><img alt=\"Party Battle\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"30\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"D012 Party Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"D012_Party_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/5f/D012_Party_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/30?cb=20121006224522\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/7a/Dissicon_ff8_Squ1.png/revision/latest?cb=20101120015408\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Assist character\"><img alt=\"Assist character\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"34\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"Dissicon ff8 Squ1.png\" data-image-key=\"Dissicon_ff8_Squ1.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/7a/Dissicon_ff8_Squ1.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/34?cb=20101120015408\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">6\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/f/fc/DFF_Potion.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203235732\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Potion\"><img alt=\"Potion\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"21\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Potion.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Potion.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/f/fc/DFF_Potion.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/21?cb=20110203235732\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">7\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Jump over the first enemy to get to D4, and Multichain to get them all. Not only is there an Expert enemy to deal with, but the Party enemies are higher level too, not Expert levels but a bit tougher than the Hard ones up to this point. Great time to use that last EX Charge. The KP Chance is a 90 second win, prepare the appropriate summon(s) for the Party and Expert foes before using the chain, and the bonus line is 16. Notice most characters seem to end their stories at Level 16 or 15? Or maybe it's just me.\n</p><p>First two are Normal enemies and thus easy, an Imaginary Champion with Sudden Cruelty and Heaven's Light, and a Delusory Warlock with Rising Wave and Genesis Rock. Now come the Party enemies. First, a Delusory Warlock with Rising Wave, Float System, Genesis Rock, Moogle, Phantasmal Girl Assist, and Force to Courage. Next comes a False Stalwart with Chain Cast, Moogle, an Idle Sky Pirate Assist, and Force to Courage. Now the Expert enters.\n</p><p>The Level 28 False Stalwart has what you'll come to recognize as the typical moveset for them - Lance Charge, Round Edge, Highbringer, Bardiche, Chain Cast, Twist Drill, and all of Garland's EX attacks. He's got the Alexander summon, a False Hero Assist, and two Muscle Belts powered up by 6 Near Opponent boosters and an After 45 Seconds. He's very powerful, has a lot of HP to burn through, and the Crystal World arena isn't conducive to Assist combos with Squall. Use your summon and EX Mode wisely, the AI tends to spam Chain Cast so block it, dash up and use Rush Impact to smash him. If you're lucky to slam him into the ground, call your Assist and dash down to Rush Impact him while Squall attacks, then do the Assist chase and strike with Ragnarok Blade. He's tough, but you can win. Don't worry about losing EX Mode or taking HP damage, there's a Potion to heal us up for the boss.\n</p><p>Bartz hit Level 16 from this fight and learned Solid Ascension, it starts out like Squall's Solid Barrel then ends with the Warrior of Light's Ascension to stab the opponent into the air, beginning a chase or wall rushing them, if they hit a wall. It's also Bartz's strongest move in terms of pure power. Open the chest for a Mu Fu, then approach the end piece.\n</p><p>As Bartz contemplates it was his fault Zidane was captured, Squall returns his Chocobo feather to him, and Exdeath reappears. This time however, Bartz isn't running. Both of them push their cutscene power to the max, Exdeath having his sword move with magic to fight Bartz and Bartz dual-wielding the Buster Sword and Gunblade, then settle down for a proper fight.\n</p>\n<table style=\"width: 275px; D012 article-table; text-align: center; color:black; float:right\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"font-size: larger; background:#1E90FF\" colspan=\"6\"><font color=\"white\"><b>Boss</b></font>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\" colspan=\"6\"><b><a href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Exdeath_(Dissidia_PSP)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Exdeath (Dissidia PSP)\">Exdeath</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\" colspan=\"6\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/6/63/Exdeath_Render.png/revision/latest?cb=20110519024644\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"Exdeath Render\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"100\" height=\"155\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"Exdeath Render.png\" data-image-key=\"Exdeath_Render.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/6/63/Exdeath_Render.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/100?cb=20110519024644\" /></a></span>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td width=\"33%\" colspan=\"2\"><b>HP</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" colspan=\"2\"><b>Level</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" colspan=\"2\"><b>Bravery</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td colspan=\"2\">3,064\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">25\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">321\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td colspan=\"6\"><b>Brave Attacks</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td colspan=\"6\">Reverse Polarity, Black Hole, Turn Guard Omni Block, Hurricane\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td colspan=\"6\"><b>HP Attacks</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td colspan=\"6\">Delta Attack, Almagest, Maelstrom\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td colspan=\"3\"><b>Summon</b>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><b>Difficulty</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td colspan=\"3\">Brynhildr\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"3\">1/5\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>As always, Exdeath could be one of the most challenging opponents yet, save for one trait. He's got a great accessory line-up, an Attractorb, Earring and Guardian Bangle pumped up by 7 Near Opponent boosters. Thus his Hurricane has a big boost in damage, and every time you attack him with a melee move - which of course is most of yours - he's going to get a decent defence boost. He has that Brynhildr summon again, and a Fleeting Flash Assist - contrary to the prior cutscene, Squall is still hanging around to be yours. And since last time in Cecil's story he was just a mid-boss, he's a lot tougher than last time we tangoed with him.\n</p><p>Not much I can say about him otherwise, you've fought him three times by this point, you know all the annoying tricks he has, you know that his biggest weakness is the poor AI. Exploit his Reverse Polarity spam as last time, attack while he's on equal footing to bait him into using it, neutral dodge and he'll appear in front of you, a sitting duck. He's got Turn Guard on the ground, Reel Axe can crush it but Hazard Raid is asking for him to block it, and in the air it's Omni Block. Overall, you can handle him, his blocks are annoying but you know how they work for yourself. His only new trick is Malestrom, an HP attack that has him charge for a long time, then summon a whirlwind around you wherever you are in the arena. And he can cancel it into a block too. He usually doesn't though so easy to stop.\n</p><p>With Exdeath crushed, Bartz's Chocobo feather turns into his Crystal...I'm not sure why, what emotional trial did he pass again? He learned to stop running from enemies? He was in the Land of Discord, you don't stick around to fight when about half the villains in the game are in your way. Zidane then comes back and Bartz runs off to show him the real deal this time, so even the game says he hasn't learned a thing. Confusing\n</p><p>We also unlock Report 12, which has fights to take care of.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<table class=\"toccolours\" width=\"85%\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; margin:0 auto; text-align: center\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align: center; border:solid 1px\"><b><a href=\"/story/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake\">Drake Clawfang's Dissidia 012 Walkthrough</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"10%\" style=\"border:solid 1px\" rowspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-8/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 17\">Previous page</a></b>\n</td>\n<td>\n<table width=\"100%\" style=\"text-align:center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><b><a href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Treachery_of_the_Gods\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Treachery of the Gods\">Treachery of the Gods</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/story/012-treachery/prologue-chapter-1/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 1\">Prologue / Chapter 1</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-2/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 2\">2</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-3/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 3\">3</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-4/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 4\">4</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-5/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 5\">5</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-6/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 6\">6</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-7/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 7\">7</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/epilogue/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 8\">Epilogue</a><hr />\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><b><a href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Light_to_All\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nore